    "sun": "contact that holds does not distinguish between an interest and an attachment; both are made by the same act of looking closely at something. so a fortnight of genuine curiosity about a person leaves you holding them at the resolution you took them in at, indefinitely, with no procedure for handing it back. you have gone into a subject for a season and come out unable to stop following it.",
    "moon": "the searching face cannot register this. curiosity that costs nothing is what it was built on — go, find out, move on — so the intake never slows, and nothing in the daily habit reports that the previous fourteen are still live. you keep arriving somewhere new with everyone you have ever looked at properly still in the room.",
