    "tension": "you never said anything is the sentence, and it is unanswerable, because it is accurate. there was no month where the thing was both real enough to raise and small enough to survive being raised. so people get years of a person who is easy, unbothered, never petty about anything, and then one conversation that ends the arrangement — and from where they stand those two are the same person doing something inexplicable.",
    "cost": "years of small damage go into you and nothing comes back out at the person, which makes you genuinely restful to be near — no scenes, no scorekeeping, nothing raised at the wrong hour. every time you have spoken, though, it has been terminal. your whole record of saying something is a record of endings, so the people closest to you have learned that your silence is the safe state."
