    "sun": "the resolution covers the transaction end to end. you watched somebody work out, over one evening, that you would cover it; you can date the year it went from a favour to an arrangement; you know which of them checks how you are and which asks how you are on the way to asking for something. none of that has ever slowed the giving by an hour.",
    "moon": "seeing where the line should sit does not put one there. a place with no edges cannot show a person the moment they crossed something, and the haze that feeds supplies no rim to do it with. so the reading and the flow run in parallel, never touching: an exact account of what is going out, kept by the one party with no instrument for stopping it.",
    "pull": "you saw each arrangement form, priced it correctly, and went on paying. the sympathy available for this is reserved entirely for people who did not notice, and you do not qualify.",
    "tension": "the polite word is generous and the honest one is soft touch, and both assume you could not tell. that assumption is what makes the whole thing bearable to everyone else, including the ones taking, and correcting it would require saying out loud that you priced the arrangement on the first night and stayed. the friendly account stands, unchallenged, and it fits a person who was fooled, which was never the person doing this.",
    "cost": "you can name, without hesitating, which three of the eleven would still be around if there were nothing coming out of you, and you are right about all three. the accuracy buys nothing. it removes the comfortable version — the one where you were used by people you trusted — and leaves you feeding a list you have already read correctly, on purpose, every week."
