    "sun": "rooms meet a person who is already ahead of them. the question gets answered before it is finished, the drink is already poured, the subject they were steering toward has been dropped for them. at ordinary strength this is thoughtfulness. at this strength people arrive somewhere and find their evening prepared by someone who read it off them in the doorway, and there is no lower setting to receive them at.",
    "moon": "nothing rests between rooms. you come home from a day of reading forty people and the same gain is pointed at your own kitchen, and what it takes there keeps as well as everything else — a thing your father said at a birthday dinner is available tonight at its original clarity, along with what his face did before he said it. no part of you argues it down later.",
    "pull": "the noticing and the keeping are one movement, doubled, with nothing set against either — so the people you have read most closely are the ones you will least be able to put down.",
    "tension": "you keep score is the charge, and it is wrong in a way that cannot usefully be corrected. no scoring happens. nothing is written down, no evening is spent going over it — the thing simply stayed, in full, the way everything stays. explaining that lands worse than the accusation. the version where you are petty is the one you take, because the accurate one describes a person nobody can live opposite.",
    "cost": "the whole of a person stays available in you — the good years and the fortnight they were unforgivable, at one clarity, neither cancelling the other, which almost nobody manages past the first serious injury. the ones you love are held at that resolution permanently. there is no evening off from it, no version of them you get to enjoy unread, and no version of you that stops."
