    "moon": "the eldest cannot notice a thing and leave it lying there. what you catch becomes yours the moment you catch it — the flinch at the door is now something you are answerable for, whether or not you were ever told what caused it. so every reading arrives already assigned. it goes in, it stays, and it stays as a duty nobody handed over and nobody will take back.",
    "pull": "nobody has been unguarded in front of you since you were thirty, and you hold, on every person in that building, an exact record of how they arrange themselves before they reach you.",
    "tension": "nobody brings the ordinary version to the top of a building, so the account you build on each of them is an account of people managing you, and it reads badly because the material was never anything else. suspicious is what comes back, from juniors who have seen the read come out right more often than is comfortable. nobody above you can say otherwise, and each year it gets a little more accurate and a little less fair.",
    "cost": "you can tell inside a minute which person at the table has already decided and is presenting otherwise, and you are right about that more often than the room would enjoy. the reading is exact and the sample is composed. what stays in you, permanently, at full clarity, is thirty people's careful handling of a senior, and no hour of anyone being ordinary near you."
