    "sun": "a question from you is a procedure. you ask why the second batch went out late and three people cancel their evening, because the eldest asking why is the beginning of something and everyone has watched where those end. nothing you look into stays small. the looking goes down through a structure you laid, floor by floor, toward the year you laid it, with nobody standing over the work to call it far enough.",
    "moon": "nothing in you settles for a good-enough answer. the descent has one setting, and whose hand is at the bottom makes no difference to it. so it gets there — your decision, in year two, on information nobody has any more — and it arrives without softening, and takes that apart with the same care it took the five above it. no desk exists to appeal the finding to.",
    "pull": "the bottom of every failure here is a decision of yours. you are the one person who will dig that far, and the one person nobody can call off.",
    "tension": "the ones who call you relentless think they are describing an inquiry into them, and the thing coming up is yours. a manager resigned last year at the third question. you were two questions from the cause that would have cleared her, and she read your interest as a finished judgement — correctly, for anyone else who could have been asking — and went before the part that let her off.",
    "cost": "nothing here breaks the same way twice, which very few places can claim, because the real cause gets found and gets said out loud. the floor has adapted: explanations arrive pre-assembled, better assembled every year, so the digging now begins a layer lower than it used to. and the thing at the bottom has your name on it, with no desk above yours to hand it up to."
