    "sun": "a space left by the eldest is not read as a space. seniority gives everything you do a direction, including the things you deliberately do not do, so an unfilled slot on a page acquires a shape — the shape people think you meant — and the shape is more binding than an instruction, because an instruction can at least be queried at the door.",
    "moon": "what you offer is room with nothing already in it, which is the rarest thing anybody hands out and worth having. it arrives with your rank on it. the room is furnished before anybody gets there — furnished with a reading of you, by people doing their honest best, and handed back to you as independence somebody exercised.",
    "pull": "the freest brief in the building comes from you, and everything that comes back through it is yours. twenty years, and nobody has shown you what they would have done.",
    "tension": "nobody who has worked for you would call you controlling, and they are right — the brief goes out open and it comes back however it comes back and you sign it. what does not get described is the week in between, which is spent on you: on a decision of yours from the spring, on what you did not say at the meeting. the effort is enormous. the subject of it is the trouble.",
    "cost": "a person two levels down can run something whole here, with real scope, at an age where most places would not let them near it. what they learn from running it is you. the ones who came up under you can predict you to the word, and what they cannot do is show you a method that is theirs."
