    "tension": "perceptive is the polite version; the other one is that nothing gets past you, which people say with a small laugh and then watch their phrasing for the rest of the meeting. so the editing tightens. every year you get better at this and every year the material gets more careful, and the two have been racing for most of your working life. the plainest thing anybody says to you now is what a stranger says in a taxi.",
    "cost": "you can tell which of two accounts is the real one inside a minute, and it is why the place has never been run on a lie for long. the instrument was built on people who could not afford to be plain with you. it reads the careful beautifully and has almost no practice on anybody speaking freely, which is the case you meet at home."
