    "sun": "everywhere else, what stays out of view stays there against somebody's authority to look — an audit, a superior, a person whose job is asking. nothing of that kind has been above you since your twenties. so the keeping has never been tested against a right to know, and what goes in was decided by one person at speed, in good faith, with the whole matter closed by the same hour.",
    "moon": "the covering finishes before anybody has formed a view on whether it should. a bad decade of somebody's went under inside a fortnight of your hearing about it, whole, and the single upright holding it is a post with a start date and an end printed on it. four people are dry under there. what they are dry under is a job.",
    "pull": "everything you have kept off the record is standing on a post, and the post has a leaving date. the people underneath think they are under a person.",
    "tension": "they call you discreet and mean it kindly, with no notion of the scale. what is absent is a mechanism rather than any lack of trust — so the count only rises, and nothing has ever come out of the covered pile, because taking something out would need a second person's judgement and at this altitude there is no second person. two people asked, years ago, were answered warmly, and did not ask again.",
    "cost": "a thing goes beyond reach here and stays there, permanently, which very few people can promise and mean, because nobody in the building is placed to make you produce it. the same absence covers the ones that should have come out years ago. they sit in with the rest, aging quietly, indistinguishable from the ones that were right, and nobody including you has looked since."
