    "moon": "holding both is not a strain from in here. each account is entire where it sits, and the two do not press on each other. what the fork will not produce is the sentence they are both waiting for: sooner or later each of them asks which version you believe, and the answer that would settle it has never assembled in you.",
    "pull": "both halves of it are in you, entire and undisputed, and the one person who can never put them side by side is the person holding both.",
    "tension": "even-handed is the early description and it is meant well. it does not survive the moment somebody needs you on their side of a table — a hearing, a wedding, a split where the money is real. what you produce then is the same steadiness you produced for both of them in private, and steadiness at that hour reads as cowardice, and the reading holds afterwards for everyone who was in the room.",
    "cost": "a person who has lied about the whole business everywhere else gives you the accurate version, since nothing in you is going to be reorganised around it — and both of them do this, so the complete matter is in one place. it buys nothing on either side. at the hour somebody needs a person who is simply theirs, everyone near you has learned this is not carried here."
